From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Stoeckmann <tobias@stoeckmann.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:25:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tar: Check if pathname exists during writing

The entry pathname can be NULL if the input string cannot be converted.
See archive_entry_pathname for more details.

If that happens, reject the entry instead of eventually running into
NULL pointer dereferences.

Signed-off-by: Tobias Stoeckmann <tobias@stoeckmann.org>

[Grape: upstream b59b9e16 (PR #3696, merged 8c4d7d77 2026-10-18).
Changed from upstream: the NULL-name guard is placed outside the
"#if defined(HAVE_REGEX_H) || ... HAVE_PCRE2POSIX_H" block, so it is
compiled in builds without a regex library (MSVC with
POSIX_REGEX_LIB=NONE). Upstream still has it inside the #if at
master 0490256c.]
---
 tar/util.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tar/util.c b/tar/util.c
index 42b08a6..fffbc83 100644
--- a/tar/util.c
+++ b/tar/util.c
@@ -426,7 +426,15 @@ edit_pathname(struct bsdtar *bsdtar, struct archive_entry *entry)
 #if defined(HAVE_REGEX_H) || defined(HAVE_PCREPOSIX_H) || defined(HAVE_PCRE2POSIX_H)
 	char *subst_name;
 	int r;
+#endif
 
+	/* Check if entry pathname can be processed. */
+	if (name == NULL) {
+		lafe_warnc(0, "Archive entry has empty or unreadable filename ... skipping");
+		return 1;
+	}
+
+#if defined(HAVE_REGEX_H) || defined(HAVE_PCREPOSIX_H) || defined(HAVE_PCRE2POSIX_H)
 	/* Apply user-specified substitution to pathname. */
 	r = apply_substitution(bsdtar, name, &subst_name, 0, 0);
 	if (r == -1) {
